cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RelyFetal: Reliability-aware single-channel fetal QRS detection"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ngo"
    given-names: "Binh Minh"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Information Technology, Ton Duc Thang University"
    city: "Ho Chi Minh City"
    country: "VN"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bminhnemhoi/nckhsv_tdtu2026-2027"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline for detecting fetal QRS complexes from single-channel
  abdominal electrocardiography, together with the experimental evidence behind
  every design decision. The central result is a three-tier contribution
  decomposition showing that the signal front-end contributes +11.00 macro F1
  points while the choice of network architecture family, at fixed temporal
  context, contributes only +0.41 points and is not statistically significant
  (paired Wilcoxon, p = 0.7012). The repository also documents a bimodal
  cross-dataset failure mode that motivates a persistent-homology signal-quality
  index with a reject option.
keywords:
  - fetal electrocardiography
  - fetal QRS detection
  - single-channel source separation
  - temporal convolutional network
  - signal quality index
  - persistent homology
  - topological data analysis
  - reproducible research
